From d165a2a7712995b7d2db6d13e9992b40681d0d45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Rezende <tricio777@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:33:32 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] feat: conditional questions server side (port of
 nextcloud/forms#3833)

Port of the server side of nextcloud/forms#3833 at head
9999a7f4478d4f3d88bd3c209a0c8a9cc0172b57 onto Forms v5.3.5:

- extraSettings `goTo` (radio, dropdown) and `next` (short, long, file,
  color, ranking, grid), validated by areExtraSettingsValid()
- updateQuestion rejects targets of other forms (400) and removes back
  jumps and jumps of missing options; reorder, clone and option delete
  remove back/stale jumps; all report `X-Forms-Adjusted: removed-jumps=(...)`
- form copy and user-migration import map targets and option ids
  (export now keeps option ids, as upstream since #3884)
- the submission path follows the jumps: only questions on it are
  validated and required, answers to skipped questions are not stored
- tests/fixtures/jump-paths.json shared with the front end

Server parts of the upstream fixes split out of #3833, ported because
#3833's code or tests rely on them: #3870 (isShownToRespondents, without
the linear-scale boolean check), #3913 (its title regex), #3904
(isListOfValues), #3916 (isOtherAnswer, option checks with "Other"),
#3903 (normalizeNumericOptionId only accepts canonical ids; grid column
part not ported).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
