From 5fde9498b2ab924c031d96b71630882c4462d403 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Rezende <tricio777@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:49:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] feat: conditional questions submit view

Port of the respondent side of nextcloud/forms#3833 at head
9999a7f4478d4f3d88bd3c209a0c8a9cc0172b57 onto Forms v5.3.5 (Options API,
mixins instead of upstream's composables):

- src/utils/Jumps.ts: upstream file, only the types path differs
  (src/models/Entities.d.ts); FormsQuestion, FormsJump, FormsJumpTarget
  and goTo/next added to the 5.3.5 types
- the submit view shows only the questions on the path, keeps a skipped
  question alive (KeepAlive) so its state comes back, announces added and
  skipped questions in a polite live region, and sends no answers for
  skipped questions
- editing a submission: a question with jumps per answer whose earlier
  answer the form no longer offers becomes required and shows "Your
  earlier answer is no longer available. Choose again."; the "form has
  changed" dialog then focuses it
- QuestionMixin: answerError prop overrides the validation error, which a
  deactivated question clears; QuestionShort clears its pending validation
  and custom validity when skipped (one debounce per question)
- edit of a grid answer parses the stored JSON (as upstream), so the
  edited submission is accepted
- tests/javascript/jumps.test.mjs runs tests/fixtures/jump-paths.json
  (npm run test:jumps), the same cases PHPUnit runs

